{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem and submitted the mitigation. The submission endpoint returned `200 Submission received`. I haven't seen the validation result.\n\n**Cause:** The `search` deployment's pod template had a stray label, `service-route: frontend`. The `frontend` service selects pods by that label, so it was sending a share of user requests to the `search` pod. That pod doesn't serve port 5000.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the label from the `search` deployment with `kubectl patch`. The `frontend` service now has only the frontend pod as its endpoint. The `search` service still points at the new `search` pod.\n\nI didn't run any test requests against the frontend after the fix."}}
